      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned child process immediately before that process starts**.\n\nSpecifically, the page describes this flow:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected only into the **environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process** \u2014 right before the process starts\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated and never holds the credential\n\nThe same pattern applies to the Query agent as well \u2014 it receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, not inherited from the Hub.\n\nThe design ensures that a compromised Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5190,
      "output_tokens": 190
    }
